w: 1.~By grace I'm saved, grace free and bound- less; My soul, be- lieve and doubt it not;
w: 2.~By grace! None dare lay claim to mer- it; Our works and con- duct have no worth,
w: 3.~By grace! O, mark this word of pro- mise When thou art by thy sins op- pressed,
w: 4.~By grace His Son, on earth ap- pear- ing, Vouch- safed be- neath thy woe to bend; 
w: 5.~By grace! This ground of faith is cer- tain; So long as God is true, it stands.
w: 6.~By grace! but think not, thou who liv- est Se- cure- ly on in god- less ways,
w: 7.~By grace! They who have heard this sen- tence Must bid hy- po- cri- sy fare- well;
w: 8.~By grace the ti- mid hearts that lan- guish, Find ac- cess to the Fa- ther's heart,
w: 9.~By grace! on this in death I'll rest me, Re- joic- ing e'en though feel- ing naught;
w: 10.~By grace! O sin and Sa- tan hear it! I bear my flag of faith in hand,
