w: Why stag- ger at this word of pro- mise? Hath Scrip- ture ev- er false- hood taught?
w: God in His love sent our Re- deem- er, Christ Je- sus, to this sin- ful earth;
w: When Sa- tan plagues thy troub- led con- science, And when thy heart is seek- ing rest.
w: Hadst thou, dam- na- tion just- ly fear- ing, Done aught to ren- der Him thy friend? 
w: What saints have penned by in- spi- ra- tion, What in His Word our God com- mands,
w: That thou, though all are called, re- cei- vest The pro- mised rest that wakes our praise:
w: For on- ly af- ter deep re- pen- tance The soul what grace im- ports can tell;
w: When con- flicts fierce and bit- ter an- guish Bid all their joy and hopes de- part.
w: I know my sin it oft op- pressed me But Him, too, who my soul hath bought:
w: And pass, in spite of doubts, nor fear it, The Red Sea to the pro- mised land;
