w: Nay; then this word must true re- main: By grace thou, too, shalt Heav'n ob- tain.
w: His death did for our sins a- tone, And we are saved by grace a- lone.
w: What rea- son can- not com- pre- hend God by His grace to thee doth send.
w: Was't not that He thy wel- fare sought, And but by grace de- liv'r- ance wrought? 
w: What our whole faith must rest up- on, Is grace a- lone, grace in His Son.
w: By grace none find in heaven a place Who live in sin in hope of grace.
w: To sin while grace a tri- fle seems, To faith it bright with glo- ry beams.
w: Where, of- times, should I strength ob- tain, Bid grace my an- chor not re- main!
w: My heart e- xults grief flees a- pace Be- cause my soul is saved by grace.
w: I hold the word my Sa- vior taught As cer- tain, whe- ther felt or not.
